    "outputShape": "On success: body with Amadeus Flight Offers Search results (offers/itineraries/pricing). On failure: body.success=false + body.error (e.g. \"Amadeus API error: ...\" or zod validation issues in body.issues[]).",
    "quirks": [
      "Body is the Amadeus Flight Offers Search v2 shape, NOT a flat {origin,destination,date}. Required arrays: originDestinations[] (with originLocationCode/destinationLocationCode/departureDateTimeRange.date), travelers[] (with id + travelerType:'ADULT'), and sources:['GDS']. A flat body 400s with body.issues[] naming the missing arrays.",
      "Charge-on-error: you are billed (~$0.032) even when the upstream Amadeus call fails (HTTP 400 with body.success=false). Same pattern as sibling flightaware endpoints.",
      "Test query (SFO->JFK 2026-07-15) returned 'Amadeus API error: Unknown error' despite a schema-valid body — route forwards correctly but upstream Amadeus availability may error; try a different/near-term date or route."
    ],
    "needs": [],
    "needsApproval": false,
    "guide": "Pay-per-call x402 (~$0.03 on Base USDC, no API key). POST a full Amadeus Flight Offers Search v2 body to https://stabletravel.dev/api/flights/availability: send originDestinations:[{id:'1',originLocationCode,destinationLocationCode,departureDateTimeRange:{date:'YYYY-MM-DD'}}], travelers:[{id:'1',travelerType:'ADULT'}], and sources:['GDS']. Read offers from the JSON body on success; on failure check body.success===false and body.error (or body.issues[] for schema problems). Note you are charged even when Amadeus returns an error, so use a valid near-term route/date.",
